INSERT INTO `forensic_analysis` VALUES (1,10,9,'Cellebrite UFED (mobile data extraction)\r\n\r\nAutopsy (analysis of extracted files)\r\n\r\nWrite-blocker setup for imaging','Device powered on in controlled lab environment.\r\n\r\nLogical extraction performed using UFED.','WhatsApp database successfully extracted.\r\n\r\nCall logs show 15 outgoing calls between Jan 05–Jan 08, 2026.','Evidence integrity preserved during acquisition.\r\n\r\nExtracted data is relevant to Case CASE-0005.\r\n\r\nChain of custody maintained in line with Malaysian Forensic SOPs.\r\n\r\nDevice contents transferred securely to lab repository for further analysis.','2026-01-12 23:23:22','2026-01-13 20:43:34',0),(2,11,9,'- FTK Imager (disk imaging)\r\n- X-Ways Forensics (file system analysis)\r\n- Write-blocker hardware\r\n\r\n','- Hard disk imaged using FTK Imager in a controlled lab environment.\r\n- Extracted image mounted in X-Ways for review.\r\n- Integrity verified with SHA-256 hash values.','- Drive contained 5 folders and 32 video files.\r\n- CCTV footage dated Jan 05–Jan 08, 2026 recovered.','- Evidence integrity preserved during acquisition and analysis.\r\n- CCTV footage relevant to Case CASE-0006.\r\n- Chain of custody maintained according to Malaysian Forensic SOPs.\r\n- Hard disk contents securely transferred to lab repository for further examination.','2026-01-13 21:02:33','2026-01-13 21:02:54',1),(3,12,9,'- FTK Imager (disk imaging)\r\n\r\n- Autopsy (browser history and email analysis)','- Laptop imaged using FTK Imager.\r\n\r\n- Extracted data imported into Autopsy for review.\r\n\r\n- Integrity verified with SHA-256 hash values.','- Browser history shows multiple visits to encrypted email services.\r\n\r\n- Email client contained 25 messages exchanged between Jan 05–Jan 10, 2026.\r\n\r\n- One deleted email successfully recovered.','- Evidence integrity preserved during acquisition.\r\n\r\n- Extracted data relevant to Case CASE-0007.\r\n\r\n- Chain of custody maintained according to Malaysian Forensic SOPs.','2026-01-13 22:30:19','2026-01-13 22:30:28',1),(4,14,9,'- Cellebrite UFED (mobile data extraction)\r\n- Autopsy (log and message review)','- Device imaged using Cellebrite UFED in a controlled lab environment.\r\n- Extracted data imported into Autopsy for analysis.\r\n\r\nIntegrity verified with SHA-256 hash values.','- 45 call logs recovered, including multiple calls to known associates.\r\n- 120 WhatsApp messages extracted, with several referencing meeting locations.','- Evidence integrity preserved during acquisition and analysis.\r\n- Extracted mobile data is relevant to Case CASE-0009.\r\n- Chain of custody maintained according to Malaysian Forensic SOPs.\r\n- Device contents securely archived in lab repository for further review.','2026-01-24 20:42:46','2026-01-24 21:51:49',1),(5,9,9,'','','','','2026-01-24 21:54:13','2026-01-24 21:54:13',0),(6,15,9,'- Wireshark (packet capture review)\r\n- Splunk (log analysis)','- Router logs exported from suspect’s office network.\r\n- Imported into Splunk for structured log analysis.\r\n- Network traffic reviewed using Wireshark.\r\n- Integrity verified with SHA-256 hash values.','- Multiple failed login attempts detected between Jan 17–18, 2026.\r\n- Suspicious IP addresses traced to external networks.\r\n- Evidence shows repeated unauthorized access attempts.\r\n- No signs of log tampering detected.','- Evidence integrity preserved during acquisition and analysis.\r\n- Network logs are relevant to Case CASE-0010.\r\n- Chain of custody maintained according to Malaysian Forensic SOPs.\r\n- Logs securely archived for examiner review.','2026-01-25 04:34:35','2026-01-25 04:34:42',1),(7,16,9,'- Autopsy (v4.20.0): Digital forensics platform used for deep file system analysis.\r\n\r\n- FTK Imager (v4.5.1): Tool used to acquire the bit-stream forensic image of the physical drive.\r\n\r\n- EnCase Endpoint Security: For memory forensics (RAM analysis).\r\n\r\n- HashCalc (v2.0): To verify SHA-256 data integrity hashes.\r\n\r\n- Tableau T35es (Write-Blocker): Physical hardware used to prevent data writing to the original drive.','1. Preparation: A clean, sterile forensic workstation was set up, and the Tableaus T35es physical write-blocker was initialized and verified.\r\n\r\n2. Image Acquisition: The hard drive was removed from the Dell XPS 15 laptop. FTK Imager was used to acquire an exact (bit-stream) forensic image of the drive into an E01 (EnCase) file format. A validation SHA-256 hash was generated at completion.\r\n\r\n3. Hash Verification: The hash of the newly acquired forensic image was verified against the MD5 hash generated during initial evidence logging. They matched, confirming integrity.\r\n\r\n4. Forensic Analysis: The forensic image was loaded into Autopsy and EnCase. The analysis focused on user activity logs, browser history, recently accessed files, and deleted data.','- Browser Activity (Google Chrome): The suspect’s browser history showed repeated visits to the \"DarkNet\" and forums discussing credit card skimming techniques on the date of 2026-03-20.\r\n\r\n- Deleted Files: Three encrypted containers (named backup1.vol, backup2.vol, and key_vault.log) were recovered from the $Recycle.Bin that had been deleted on 2026-03-22 at 09:15 AM (approx. 30 minutes before the search warrant execution).\r\n\r\n- Registry Analysis: The Windows Registry analysis showed evidence that a USB storage device named \"Lexar 32GB\" was plugged in on 2026-03-21 at 23:30. This device was not found during the physical search.\r\n\r\n- Email Communication: Several outgoing emails with encrypted attachments were found, timestamped from March 18th to March 21st. The contents remain unreadable without decryption keys.','Based on the forensic analysis of Case ID: CASE-0011, there is strong evidence to suggest the suspect was actively engaged in research and communication regarding digital financial fraud and credit card skimming. The recovery of deleted, encrypted containers from the workstation confirms attempts to conceal data prior to the search. The verification of the Lexar USB drive indicates a potential missing piece of evidence. The forensic integrity of the analysis was maintained at every step, with all actions and findings formally documented and anchored in the ForenChain ledger.','2026-03-23 09:46:25','2026-03-23 09:46:34',1),(8,17,9,'- Cellebrite UFED 4PC: For high-level mobile data extraction and bypassing screen locks.\r\n- MSAB Raven: Used for field-triage of mobile application data.\r\n- Magnet AXIOM Cyber: To reconstruct deleted chat databases and timeline analysis.\r\n- Faraday Shielded Enclosure: To maintain RF isolation during the extraction process.','1. RF Isolation: The device was transferred from the portable Faraday bag to a permanent shielded lab enclosure to ensure no remote signal (wipe command) could reach the device.\r\n\r\n2. Advanced Logical Extraction: Due to the iPhone\'s hardware encryption, an \"Advanced Logical\" extraction was performed to pull all accessible SQLite databases (Messages, Calls, Apps).\r\n\r\n3. Media Carving: Automated tools were used to \"carve\" through the unallocated space to recover thumbnails of deleted images.\r\n\r\n4. Verification: The resulting .ufdr report file was hashed and the value was automatically sent to the ForenChain smart contract.','- Encrypted Communication: Found an installed \"Signal\" messaging app. While the app was locked, notification logs recovered from the system file show a message received on 2026-03-22 stating: \"The hardware is in the trunk of the silver sedan.\"\r\n\r\n- Geofencing Data: Apple Maps \"Significant Locations\" cache shows the device was at the Batu Kawan Industrial Park area four times between March 15th and March 20th.\r\n\r\n- Deleted Media: Recovered a deleted screenshot of a bank transfer confirmation for RM 15,000 to an offshore account. The screenshot was deleted 5 minutes before the \"Airplane Mode\" was activated.','The forensic examination of FC-2026-005M provides objective evidence of coordinated activity. The recovered notification logs and geofencing data directly link the suspect to the primary crime scene locations. The attempted destruction of the bank transfer screenshot suggests \'Guilty Knowledge\' and intent to conceal financial trails. All extracted data has been verified for integrity, and the forensic image is now archived in the secure evidence vault. Investigation Status: Evidence Highly Relevant.','2026-03-27 11:47:04','2026-03-27 11:47:45',1),(9,18,9,'- Autopsy (IoT Module): For parsing cloud-synced SQLite databases.\r\n- Wireshark: To capture outgoing traffic to Amazon AWS servers before disconnection.\r\n- CROWD (Cloud Retrieval of Online Web Data): To pull synced Alexa voice history.','1. Network Isolation: Moved to a controlled network environment to prevent a remote \"Factory Reset\" command.\r\n2. Cloud Extraction: Used the suspect\'s authenticated session tokens (recovered from Case 0011\'s laptop) to legally pull the last 48 hours of voice command logs.\r\n3. Internal Storage: Performed a logical acquisition of the onboard flash memory.','- Voice Logs: A voice command was recorded on 2026-03-21 at 22:45: \"Alexa, how do I wipe a hard drive quickly?\" * Motion Sensor Data: The Echo Show\'s built-in camera logged motion in the kitchen at 03:00 AM on the night of the incident, despite the suspect claiming they were asleep.\r\n- Linked Devices: The Echo hub was linked to a hidden smart lock on the back door that was opened at 03:05 AM.','The IoT forensics for CASE-0013 successfully places the suspect at the scene during the time of the crime. The voice command history demonstrates \'premeditated intent\' to destroy digital evidence. Evidence is verified and synced to the blockchain.','2026-03-27 13:23:18','2026-03-27 13:23:20',1),(10,20,9,'- Chainalysis Reactor: For tracing the movement of funds on the Bitcoin and Ethereum blockchains.\r\n- Ledger Live (Forensic Mode): To verify public addresses associated with the hardware.\r\n- Bitcoin Core Node: For local verification of transaction timestamps on the mainnet.','1. Public Key Extraction: Extracted the Extended Public Key (xPub) to view the entire transaction history without needing the private keys.\r\n\r\n2. Blockchain Correlation: Matched the outgoing transactions from this wallet to a reported \"phishing attack\" that occurred on 2026-01-10.\r\n\r\n3. Address Clustering: Identified that the stolen funds were moved through a \"Mixer\" service before 0.5 BTC was sent to a known exchange account belonging to the suspect.','- Transaction History: The wallet contains a balance of 2.45 BTC and 15.2 ETH.\r\n\r\n- Timestamp Match: A transaction for 0.5 BTC occurred exactly 12 minutes after the suspect logged into the Dell Laptop (Case 0011).\r\n\r\n- Seed Phrase: The recovered 24-word phrase was confirmed to grant full access to the funds identified in the phishing report.','The analysis of FC-2026-021W provides the \'smoking gun\' for the financial motive in this case. By tracing the on-chain movement of funds, we have linked the physical hardware found in the suspect\'s safe to the digital theft reported three months ago. The synchronisation of timestamps between the laptop logs and the blockchain transactions creates an irrefutable link. Case data is anchored to ForenChain for trial.','2026-03-27 16:37:31','2026-03-27 16:38:21',1),(11,21,9,'VOT (Visual Online Tool): For decoding proprietary DJI flight DAT files.\r\n\r\nCellebrite Premium: To access the onboard encrypted storage.\r\n\r\nGoogle Earth Pro: To map and visualise the recovered GPS coordinates.','1. Physical Inspection: Checked for any modified hardware or \"payload\" attachments (none found).\r\n\r\n2. Log Acquisition: Extracted flight controller logs which contain GPS, altitude, and pilot control inputs.\r\n\r\n3. Media Recovery: Recovered 4K video footage from the MicroSD card, including several \"Home Point\" locations.','Flight Path: The flight log shows the drone took off from a park exactly 1.2km away from the facility at 22:15 UTC.\r\n\r\nHome Point: The \"Return to Home\" (RTH) coordinate matches the suspect’s registered home address found in Case 0011.\r\n\r\nVideo Evidence: The camera was active and recording during the entire flight, capturing high-resolution images of the facility\'s security checkpoints.','The forensic analysis of FC-2026-030D provides undeniable proof of unauthorised surveillance. The flight path and \'Home Point\' metadata create a direct digital link between the drone and the suspect. This data, combined with the video files recovered, supports the charge of \'Espionage\' and \'restricted airspace violation\'. Metadata and hashes have been committed to the ForenChain block.','2026-03-30 08:27:15','2026-03-30 08:29:06',1),(12,22,9,'- Magnet AXIOM Cyber: For parsing SQLite databases (Health, Messages, Locations).\r\n- iBrave / Cellebrite: To perform a \"Full File System\" extraction via the diagnostic port.\r\n- Google Earth Pro: To visualise the recovered GPS coordinates from the \"Workouts\" app.','1. Isolation: Transferred device from the Faraday pouch to a shielded forensic workstation.\r\n2. Bypass: Used the pre-authenticated session (unlocked state) to perform a Logical and File System extraction.\r\n3. Synchronization: Correlated heart rate timestamps with the system clock of the suspect’s iPhone (Case-0012).\r\n4. Hashing: Generated a SHA-256 hash of the extracted .zip archive to anchor on ForenChain.','- Biometric Date: Heart rate increased from 72 BPM to 148 BPM at exactly 03:02:15 AM on 31/03/2026.\r\n- Activity Tracking: The \"Health\" app recorded a sudden burst of activity (running) lasting 4 minutes during the same window.\r\n- GPS Triggers: The last recorded GPS \"Home Point\" sync matches the crime scene perimeter (Bayan Lepas), despite the suspect\'s claim of being at home in Simpang Ampat.','The biometric and location data recovered from FC-041W provides a high-confidence link to the crime scene. The physiological stress indicators (Heart Rate) match the exact timestamp of the Smart Home breach (Case-0013). The suspect\'s physical activity at 03:00 AM contradicts all prior statements. Analysis complete; findings hashed to the immutable ledger.','2026-03-30 19:29:34','2026-03-30 19:29:42',1),(13,23,9,'- FTK Imager: Used for bit-stream physical imaging and generating the primary E01 file.\r\n- Tableau T8u USB 3.0 Bridge: A hardware Write-Blocker to ensure zero data alteration.\r\n- Autopsy / Sleuth Kit: For keyword searching and carving through unallocated space.','1. Hardware Integrity: Connected the drive via a Tableau Write-Blocker; verified that the \"Read-Only\" light was active.\r\n2. Physical Imaging: Created a bit-for-bit clone (E01) of the 2TB drive to preserve the original state.\r\n3. Data Carving: Ran automated scripts to recover files from \"Unallocated Space\" (files that the suspect thought were deleted).\r\n4. Hashing: Verified that the MD5 and SHA-1 hashes of the image matched the drive\'s initial state.','- Hidden Partitions: Discovered an 80GB hidden encrypted partition (TrueCrypt) labelled \"System_Vault\".\r\n- Deleted Records: Successfully recovered a deleted spreadsheet titled EXFIL_LOG_2026.xlsx.\r\n','The forensic image of FC-055S contains the \'Missing Link\' for this investigation. The recovered data matches the stolen intellectual property from the victim\'s server. The presence of hidden partitions suggests an intentional effort by the suspect to conceal the stolen assets. Extraction complete; all digital evidence is hashed and locked to ForenChain.','2026-03-30 20:59:01','2026-03-30 20:59:04',1),(14,24,9,'- Berla iVe / Chip-off extraction','- Performed a direct hardware chip-off to bypass the Tesla OS password and access raw NAND data.','Recovered Bluetooth connection logs for the suspect\'s iPhone (Case-0012) at 03:15 AM. Found GPS waypoints leading directly to the victim’s location. The car\'s \"Sentry Mode\" also recorded video of the suspect entering the car at the time of the breach','The vehicle data provides a precise location-time matrix that places the suspect\'s car at the crime scene. Data signatures hashed to ForenChain.','2026-03-31 23:55:27','2026-03-31 23:56:11',1);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `forensic_analysis` ENABLE KEYS */;
